{"name":"Chasm","hex":"#876044","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chasm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality and provincial park in the Thompson-Nicola Regional District, British Columbia, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chasm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chasm (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Chasm is a Metroidvania video game developed and published by Bit Kid, Inc. for Microsoft Windows, macOS, Linux, PlayStation 4 and PlayStation Vita in July 2018, the Nintendo Switch in October 2018, and the Xbox One in November 2018."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6d/Chasm-game-box-art-icon.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chasm_(video_game)"},{"title":"Rift","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rift is a linear zone where the lithosphere is being pulled apart and is an example of extensional tectonics. Typical rift features are a central linear downfaulted depression, called a graben, or more commonly a half-graben with normal faulting and rift-flank uplifts mainly on one side. Where rifts remain above sea level they form a rift valley, which may be filled by water forming a rift lake. The axis of the rift area may contain volcanic rocks, and active volcanism is a part of many, but not all, active rift systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Rift_segmentation.png/330px-Rift_segmentation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rift"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/500px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/1280px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/GulfofSuezRift.png/500px-GulfofSuezRift.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gulf of Suez Rift showing main extensional faults","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGulfofSuezRift.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/FlankMalawi.png/500px-FlankMalawi.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/FlankMalawi.png/1280px-FlankMalawi.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/FlankMalawi.png/500px-FlankMalawi.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Topographic profile of Lake Malawi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlankMalawi.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg/500px-20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg/1280px-20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg/500px-20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_%2848453477346%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Volcano-tectonic landforms connected to rifting on Reykjanes Peninsula, Iceland: faults, fissures, elongated volcanoes of subglacial origin, postglacial lava fields","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A20190621_CPH-KEF_7314_(48453477346).jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}